WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:29.800
I can't imagine not creating things. It's
the most fundamental and uncomplicated joy

00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:31.800
that I can imagine.

00:00:34.820 --> 00:00:41.900
I had two grandparents who succumed to cancer,
so I'm really passionate about studying the

00:00:41.900 --> 00:00:49.960
body, the different processes that facilitate
its physiology.

00:00:49.960 --> 00:00:55.930
I love how kids can just smile. They are passionate
about everything that they're involved in,

00:00:55.930 --> 00:01:00.739
and they want to learn, and they want to grow,
and they want you to teach them. I love the

00:01:00.739 --> 00:01:04.670
life and joy that kids bring.

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:15.560
I am most passionate about my faith. I just
want to live in a way that makes others wonder

00:01:15.570 --> 00:01:17.890
who or what I'm living for.

00:01:41.130 --> 00:01:47.670
I hope to one day go back to Kenya and contribute
greatly to the field of medical research,

00:01:47.670 --> 00:01:52.850
and also provide quality medical care to Kenyan
patients.

00:01:52.850 --> 00:01:59.729
A dream of mine has always been to be a scientific illustrator, and Hillsdale has helped me see

00:01:59.729 --> 00:02:04.399
how that's attainable by giving me a strong
classical training in art, and instilling

00:02:04.399 --> 00:02:09.259
in me how important intellectual curiosity
is.

00:02:09.259 --> 00:02:15.870
Whatever I do, whether it be pursuing baseball
or a career in the business world, I just

00:02:15.870 --> 00:02:20.970
want to be the man that God wants me to be.

00:02:20.970 --> 00:02:25.709
My greatest hope for my life is that I can
be successful as a teacher, and what that

00:02:25.709 --> 00:02:30.049
means to me is that I can teach kids what
I've learned here at Hillsdale, which is how

00:02:30.060 --> 00:02:35.400
to think and how to question the world around
me, and become the best versions of themselves.

